My voice is completely ruined.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:09.120
AH!

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.520
So I thought...

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.800
If there's ever gonna be a perfect time for me to do an update vlog, it is now.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.980
Because it's gonna be chill, it's just gonna be a nice little sit-down,

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.700
and I- honestly, I am way overdue to make one of these

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.280
Obviously, I don't know if you noticed this,

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.540
but the channel has undergone some changes lately.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.579
Anyone picked up on it? *short chuckle*

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.520
But not just that- but I personally have undergone some changes lately as well,

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.680
and I haven't really addressed any of it in a video

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.740
because I've been too busy playing Minecraft. So, I thought now

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.820
would be the perfect time

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:50.399
Minecraft! *another lil laugh*

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.080
Minecraft has completely taken over,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.640
and I gotta say, I absolutely love it and it's just been so fun.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.140
There's just been so much positivity with the channel and all the content and people just

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.160
wanting more videos and feeling like "Oh, that was such a good episode. I really enjoyed that."

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.160
That for me, has been so fun to follow, and to hear from you guys.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.640
You know, when you make YouTube videos,

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:23.760
or at least gaming videos, an- and frequently at that. Sometimes you hit certain things that

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.900
maybe get really popular,

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:31.799
but maybe you don't enjoy making it yourself, or maybe some things that you really enjoy recording

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:38.250
doesn't get very popular for whatever reason or maybe people don't like it, because it doesn't translate as well, to-

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.140
into video format.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:45.720
So, it's almost like you have these different- You have these things that you want to hit as a YouTuber but-

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.009
and sometimes you hit one or two of them, but with Minecraft, it's just been everything.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.900
And its just been all positive,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.180
but the channel is getting more views than has ever gotten. Everyone seemed really happy and positive about it.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:02.280
I absolutely loved recording it. And ad revenue is absolutely fantastic! *laugh*

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:09.680
Like it could not be better. Uh- I know some people are saying "oh, he's only playing Minecraft because NOW he's getting ads."

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.700
No, I would have done it anyway, but-

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:19.020
It is epic, I'm not gonna lie. I feel like I'm finally earning what people think I'm making out of YouTube videos. *laugh*

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.320
Merch is still the best way to support the channel. (link in description) Thank you. Okay.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.849
It is funny looking back as well, because I did a

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:35.089
podcast with Cold Ones, like a month ago, or before Minecraft took off and

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.338
we were talking about like "Oh, what's the next thing gonna be like?"

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.660
*Pewdiepie in podcast:* "I wonder what the next is gonna be.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.520
"Cuz, I think people are getting tired of those type of videos."

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.280
"Yeah, well, it's hard to say, because no one wants to be the guy that makes the-

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:53.060
"Everyone wants to be the fucking follower of that. 'Let's just do what everyone else does.'"

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.060
YouTube is always changing so quickly...

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:00.460
It's pretty crazy. But, whenever my channel gets like a second wind like this for the

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:08.570
hundredth time at this point it feels like, I'm always so grateful. It just feels amazing and honestly like I can't believe-

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:14.990
I'm- I think I'm- this year is my tenth year as a YouTuber uploading every single day and

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.440
to still be on top of what I do is just

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.960
unbelievable, especially

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.860
looking back at other YouTubers at the time, you know, the longevity of YouTubers was so short.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.660
I always thought like "Oh, I could probably do it for like another year and then people won't care,"

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.940
So just still being able to make videos that I feel really good about and that my audience really like as well

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.200
is pretty crazy. When I started off

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:45.120
Uh- YouTube, I made videos for like a whole year and no one really watched it.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:52.440
I'm sure you've seen some of my older videos, YouTube liked to recommend them very specifically like my hundred subs special or whatever

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:02.080
*Pewdiepie in 100 subs special:* "And yeah today we're gonna celebrate because I got 100 subscribers, oh my lord 100 subscribers!

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.520
But once I started playing "Amnesia",

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.310
which was the thing that really took off for my channel,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.350
because I played this horror game and I was giving these little

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:21.749
objects in the game names. There was Stefano, there was the barrels, which was the enemy I mean,

00:04:21.749 --> 00:04:25.380
it's the same concepts as I'm doing now that I think about it *laughs out loud*

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:34.440
But, it was like a very endearing time for my memory and my heart at that time and

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:39.569
you know, that's what I really fell in love with YouTube doing that stuff

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:45.210
and that's when I decided I'm gonna pursue being a YouTuber because this is amazing and then you know

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:48.779
It kind of went down a lot after a while after a few years people

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:52.529
kind of got bored of scary games and so did I.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:05:00.719
So... that was a very stressful period when you're trying to transition into something else as a youtuber, so to be here again

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.360
doing the same thing like with Minecraft,

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.399
having that moment that I had when I started off,

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.429
I never thought I would relive that ever.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.280
I never thought I would experience that again.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:20.549
And I'm so happy that I get to do that with Minecraft and I feel like such a douche bag for like

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.909
Picking on this game and be like, "No, it's too popular,

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.920
I don't want to play it!" and then here I am like

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:32.960
"Oh, it's actually good." but also looking back, I feel like now was the perfect time for me to play it, you know?

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.160
It's not just about the game,

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:42.330
it's also the timing, I think at least. It feels like I've come to a full circle with a channel now,

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.449
Coming back to gaming this way and looking back

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.439
you know, it's been a rocky road and I think

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:55.649
that's almost why a lot of people appreciate the channel at this point

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:03.809
and I appreciate everyone sticking through it with me throughout like all the controversies and and all that stuff and obviously looking back now

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.810
I kind of feel like...

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.300
very stupid about it, and how a lot of it just wasn't worth it

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:18.160
So basically, I'm sorry for all the bad things I've done. I just want to play minecraft, please.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:25.029
I guess I just realized it's like- this is why I started making videos. This is what I enjoy doing.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:30.400
Obviously, I'm not gonna be able to do Minecraft forever. There's always gonna be the next thing or whatever

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:37.900
but, then again if I stop playing Minecraft, then my pet Sven is

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.050
gonna be alone and I can't let that happen.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:45.370
Another big change in-

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:50.050
for the channel has been Brad, who's been editing for- for those who don't know

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.219
I used to have two editors, Brad and Sive, Sive still working with me, but Brad

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.800
left to do his own thing.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:03.400
Brad and I have been working together for five years and we made a lot of really amazing videos that I'm really really proud of

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.420
"It's now or never!"

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:14.100
"You're wearing a life jacket BeastMaster64, should I be wearing a life jacket?" "Oh, absolutely!"

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.460
What happened?

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.640
He didn't make it...

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.880
Camera Man... he didn't make it...

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.100
The sea swallowed him.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:35.450
So now it's just me and- and Sive, and I was looking for a new editor right away,

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:39.649
but in the meanwhile, I was editing my own Minecraft episodes

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:43.730
And for those of you don't know, for five- for the first five years of me making videos,

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.069
I was editing every single day and as

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.419
tedious that can be- and as tedious and time-consuming that can be,

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:55.879
It's also something I've missed for a while and I realized while editing the Minecraft videos that

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:01.700
I actually really enjoy editing those and I can tell that you guys enjoy it as well

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:03.870
because-

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.870
instead of just-

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:08.030
trying to record the video and...

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.400
just get it up.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:14.869
Because tomorrow we have another video so it doesn't matter, you know

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.010
That's kind of the attitude

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.869
we had to keep with the frequency of the uploads on this channel and

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:25.460
Considering most of the time it's two people involved to get the video done

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.940
Instead, when when I get to edit it

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.780
I can sort of shape it in a way that makes more sense than I can really make it

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.869
Exactly how I want it and I can put that little extra effort in

00:08:37.169 --> 00:08:39.679
which a lot of times I've seen as unnecessary, but

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:44.749
It's been really fun to do that. And there's a lot of Minecraft episodes now that I-

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.459
it always sounds cringey, but I generally feel very proud of like the-

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.300
The Wither Episode

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.400
and the one with Sven's wedding and all that stupid stuff,

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.800
I love that, I think it's so fun to make that stuff and I'm very very happy with that

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.629
It's been a while since I've been able to say like "Oh, I feel really proud of this video"

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.250
So that feels really good as well

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:08.600
You know, they said what I said

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:14.640
I feel like I'm naturally coming back to where I started with this channel, and I enjoy it. I really do

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.520
Another thing is that I'm getting married soon

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.509
Marzia, I can't wait to be your husband.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:25.970
I'm very excited but it's also been a lot of work and then to also edit my own videos

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.970
It's been hard to keep up. So

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:30.270
just know, I'm trying my best

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:32.270
with the time that I have each day

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.759
for anyone that's a YouTuber that you know

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.640
it's a grind and for a lot of other businesses whenever you start something and

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.700
you reach a level of success. You can kind of like slow down a bit and

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:49.240
let other people take over the work, but to still have me here to like doing all that

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:53.920
It's kind of crazy if you think about it, but at the same time, this is what I enjoy doing

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:59.040
This is what I want to do. So I'm actually just happy about it. I think it's fun. The final thing

00:09:59.049 --> 00:10:02.300
I wanted to address now is that you know, I'm getting married, Brad's left,

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.960
Hitting 100 million subscribers, an insane number. It's the dumbest number I ever heard, but I

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.040
still have don't believe it, like before YouTube,

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:17.349
I was that weird kid with no friends and then all the sudden there's so many people that enjoy what I do

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:24.840
It's pretty insane to me. I like I still can't wrap my head around it, honestly. Thank you everyone for subscribing

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:32.120
Whether your been here since the beginning or on and off or for a little while, I really appreciate every one of you.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:40.960
There's been a lot of speculation that I'm gonna quit the channel because of all these pieces kind of falling together I

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.480
still really enjoy YouTube and

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:45.279
I have no plans of quitting

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:52.400
I do think it would be good for me to take a break at some point just to feel what it's like to have a break.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:11:00.600
Like, I don't take breaks. I just keep going and going and going because I'm so in the routine of making videos

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.610
but it would be nice to just

00:11:02.839 --> 00:11:06.548
Not have YouTube in my brain for the first time in ten years

00:11:07.399 --> 00:11:12.758
I'll probably do that at some point in the future at least but I just wanted to address the whole 'he's gonna quit' thing

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:16.329
Other than that, I just want to say I'm really happy

00:11:16.369 --> 00:11:21.579
Um, you guys seem happy as well and that just feels really good. And I think that's

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:28.260
The bottom line is that I just really enjoy making uplifting content and it was good to do that

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:35.640
So thank you everyone for watching. This has been the update vlog. Hope you enjoyed check out MERCH!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:45.260
You don't have to like honestly, but it would be epic I'll see you guys in tomorrow's video. Bye. Bye!

